<% content_for :title, "#{@addon.title} — Tinkerex" %>

<%# A migrated addon carries its markup and CSS classes across the port from its old per-addon
    controller/view into this generic shell, but the wide container was never part of the view
    BODY — the legacy Tools::BoxesController's own view opted in with this exact content_for line,
    sitting outside anything a manifest-driven port copies. Silently dropping it doesn't error: the
    page still renders, just 440px narrower, with a multi-column addon UI (a 3-column grid, a tile
    gallery) squeezed into a single column. The manifest is the one place left for an addon to ask
    for this, since the host — not the addon bundle — owns the page chrome. %>
<% content_for :container_class, "container-wide" if @addon.layout == "wide" %>

<div class="page-head"><h1><%= @addon.icon %> <%= @addon.title %></h1>
  <p class="page-subtitle muted"><%= @addon.description %></p>
</div>

<%# The whole addon UI mounts here. Every value the addon needs from the host arrives as a data
    attribute, so the bundle never has to know a Rails route or guess at context.

    `service-url` is a BASE, not a full URL to one endpoint: a bundle that talks to a sidecar (its
    manifest's own `services` entry, e.g. "boxes") builds each call as
    `${ctx.serviceUrl}${service}/${path}` — e.g. `${ctx.serviceUrl}boxes/generate`. It ends in "/"
    for exactly that reason (see `service_base_url` in Tools::AddonsController, which derives it from
    the real route rather than a hand-duplicated literal). `states-url` is a complete URL on its own
    (GET it directly) — it has no per-call path to append, unlike `service-url`. %>
<div data-controller="addon"
     data-addon-ctx-value="<%= @ctx.to_json %>"
     data-addon-entry-value="<%= tools_addon_asset_path(@addon.key, @addon.entry) %>"
     data-addon-save-url-value="<%= tools_addon_path(@addon.key) %>"
     data-addon-service-url-value="<%= @service_url %>"
     data-addon-states-url-value="<%= tools_addon_states_path(@addon.key) %>"
     data-addon-folders-value="<%= @folders.to_json %>"
     data-addon-default-folder-value="<%= @default_parent_node_id %>"
     data-addon-default-folder-label-value="<%= @default_folder_label %>"
     data-addon-children-url-value="<%= library_children_path %>"
     data-addon-create-url-value="<%= library_folders_path %>">
  <div data-addon-target="mount"></div>
</div>
